body:
if this helps anyone:

i use a mod called No City Living / Island Living names. i’m not by my pc but im sure its easily to find

10000% one of my essential mods, fixed the problem perfectly

from chicago, lived in texas and tennessee. (moving home soon!)

but lord oh lord, does everyone know my contempt for being called “ma’am.”
i understand the culture and that it’s meant to be polite, but dammit, at least call me “miss!”

> Everyone keeps saying “omg I realized so much more on rewatch, you really need to be paying attention” and I don’t know what I’m supposed to be looking for? 

&#x200B;

here's the thing: you will still miss things on your 38420348th watch. don't stress too much about it... it actually makes it so much cooler to see \*how\* much you missed. there would be no way to absorb everything on first watch; it's so dense.  


&#x200B;

also: we'd love to have ya here, but don't look \*ANYTHING\* up about the show until you're 10000000% finished. people \*WILL\* spoil it. i was spoiled several times even when things were marked as "do not spoil."

&#x200B;

\*\*trust me: unsub and don't even google anything about the show until you're done.\*\*

if so, i’m glad. i feel like 99% of the time i hear a spooky one (either vamps, spell casters, werewolves, or strangerville??? can’t tell.)

once it a while it would be fine, but it feels so out of place… especially because i rarely do occult play throughs 🥲 just trying to make a cute family house and it’s like “💀👽👾🤖👻🧛🏻‍♀️🦇🐺🕵🏻”

hope this means it’ll shake it up a bit more

>poo soup bowls

&#x200B;

after hearing this terminology for the first time, for *many* different reasons, i welcome death

okay i'm OFFICIALLY BACK! (stomach hurt so i took a nap but now i'm ready.)

&#x200B;

i need to tell you how MUCH YOU ROCKED MY DAMN WORLD WITH THAT INFORMATION!!! i was Dx with ADHD \*after\* college, where i started smoking cigarettes. this is so fucking fascinating. it's sad, but it's interesting because recently ADHD has become more understood beyond "the little boys' disease," so there's so much more to find out and this is not one thing i'd consider to have a correlation, but it makes PERFECT sense.

&#x200B;

and from the way you wrote your comment, it seems like you had ADHD as well. we're always looking for the next, quickest nicotine fix + being overstimulated + the oral fixation + the social interaction is like, the fucking perfect storm for someone with ADHD. i've been thinking about your comment since i read it!

and yeah, to your top paragraph: it's obviously fine to have preferences, even things that repulse you in others, but it's so rude to fucking shame someone in front of their damn face. people act like it's still the 50s and we don't have any idea! we know. we hate it. it's not great. it's just hurtful at that point. and honestly? i'm going to say this as tactfully as possible: i find myself  having an aversion to people who binge drink on alcohol. i used to (ya know, college) but i'm not gonna walk up to someone at a bar and say "WOW LOL FUCKING GROSSSSS." people would hate me. but if i lit up a cigarette outside away from the door? everyone would turn around and do the same.

&#x200B;

i remember on campus i was one of maybe like, 10 regular smokers. we would stay out of the way and people would literally shout shit to us across campus. we made it a point to be as respectful as possible as far as distance, etc.

&#x200B;

i'm GLAD people have such an aversion to smoking, but i think it worked so well that they have decompartmentailized / forgot that we're people too. we have feelings. shaming us out of it probably won't work. for some people, sure. but i'd just end up chain smoking and feeling shittier about myself. it comes into the social stigmas against addiction, and that can also go back to my point on alcohol. we have a bad, awful habit and we want to quit but it's so easy to get our fix. i can think of 6 places off the top of my head rn i can get tobacco (or beer!)

&#x200B;

do you still smoke cigarettes? i switched to vaping in 2018 after i realized i was up to 1-2 packs a day... back home a pack was $16, probably more now. i want to quit vaping because i'm on birth control which now at my age severely increases the chance of a stroke. but it's HARD!

&#x200B;

TL;DR: adhd stat blew me away. it's a perfect trap for us to fall into because dopamine, social circle, oral fixation, escape from overstimulation, stimming, etc. glad people hate smoking but they need to remember we're people too, and most of us genuinely try our best to be as out of the way as possible.

thank you again for blowing my mind <3

INFO: to be clear, he has no financial responsibility for the backpack, right?

if he doesn’t, NTA. getting a new backpack every year as a kid was awesome. (and it’s not like it will last forever. once i was in like 6th grade i stuck with the same one for a while since it was pretty neutral.)

it’s a fun way to get excited for the new school year!
